      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The design of electron transport layers (ETLs) is crucial to the performance of optoelectronic devices. A composite ETL was constructed to overcome the poor carrier extraction issue in perovskite solar cells, resulting in a maximum PCE of 19.14% with reduced hysteresis. A similar enhancement phenomenon was observed in both devices based on TiO2 and SnO2 ETLs."},
